/given-names></name><name><surname>Tamayo</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mesirov</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GenePattern 2.0</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><year>2006</year><volume>38</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>500</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/ng0506-500</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Reich M, Liefeld T, Gould J, Lerner J, Tamayo P, Mesirov JP (2006) GenePattern 2.0. Nat Genet 38(5):500 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16642009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Subramanian</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamayo</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mootha</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Gene set enrichment analysis: a knowledge-based approach for interpreting genome-wide expression profiles</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2005</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>15545</fpage><lpage>15555</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0506580102</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Subramanian A, Tamayo P, Mootha VK et al (2005) Gene set enrichment analysis: a knowledge-based approach for interpreting genome-wide expression profiles. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA 102:15545&#x02013;15555 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16199517</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smyth</surname><given-names>GK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Linear models and empirical Bayes methods for assessing differential expression in microarray experiments</article-title><source>Stat Appl Genet Mol Biolgy</source><year>2004</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>3</fpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Smyth GK (2004) Linear models and empirical Bayes methods for assessing differential expression in microarray experiments. Stat Appl Genet Mol Biolgy 1:3 </citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="other">Smyth GK (2005) Limma: linear models for microarray data. In: Gentleman R, Carey V, Dudoit S, Irizarry R, Huber W (eds) Bioinformatics and Computational Biology Solutions using R and Bioconductor. Springer, Heidelberg</citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>